      "id": "s06-battleship-hull-detail-2026-10-16",
      "date": "2026-10-16",
      "owner": "owner (Lukasz Jawor)",
      "decision": "approved",
      "scope_statement": "Approved the hull surface-detail revision of the Alliance Pelagic battleship - the only asset this revision changes. The owner's words were \"This looks good\", after reviewing the revision against the approved hull at capital-detail, capital-close and tactical cameras plus native-pixel crops of the bow deck and the aft machinery.",
      "approval_kind": "appearance-revision",
      "revision": {
        "asset_id": "core:alliance/battleship",
        "gameplay_binding": "rebel_battleship",
        "change": "hull surface detail: raised deck plating with edge trenches, banded bow-crown armour with strakes and machinery wells, flank armour belt with dark gaps, machinery banks, vent banks, bridge-base window bands, drive housings, ram ribs, owner-colour prow chevron and deck centre stripe",
        "source_authority": "script-authoritative",
        "triangles": {
          "before": 8701,
          "after": 11457
        },
        "silhouette_change": "length unchanged, beam grown: every detail element stands 0.5 to 4 world units proud of the surface it sits on, and at the hull's widest section - the armour belt, its dark plate gaps and the flank machinery banks at z -105 to -69 - that proud detail is the mesh's X extent, so the beam moves from 69.0 to 73.349998 and the mesh is 6.3 percent wider. The Y and Z extents are unchanged to the digit (Z -143.5 to 135.0), so the in-game length, which the renderer takes from the catalogue size policy on Z, is unchanged, and no collision or simulation field moves: radii come from the data files, not from the mesh.",
        "supersedes": {
          "assets/models/alliance_battleship.mesh.json": "57a5496c539a0252a237ef7a3671509f705308416da3f2afe0c9555ff17e9fec"
        },
        "source": {
          "art/blender/alliance_battleship.blend": "a51b636fc83f1e13b3659440f93adbb68253a6f59a5b0416c4cedc81ca57a791"
        },
        "exporter": {
          "tools/art/alliance_common.py": "7c79e480fe99b1e8950629dce9eeafcbb4e3562d3f9bbaac22d9525a19bfa057",
          "tools/art/build_alliance_battleship.py": "52380040fd04c3370085c1815e68cb520d5e54f1f4af04ac53ec69d7233d0082"
        },
        "runtime": {
          "assets/models/alliance_battleship.mesh.json": "0a4e397d5c0b60f70fbba35f3e4f4a5ac997ac4de079f821f8f29db9872c95cd"
        },
        "corrections": "This record first said the revision changed no silhouette. That held for the length and not for the beam: the mesh outgrew the envelope declared for the previous revision, and the S02 extension-contract validator noticed it while PR #117 was being made to pass again against main. The extents above are measured from the two payloads rather than reasoned from the Z extent, and the artifact itself is unchanged - this is the record catching up with the file the owner approved, not a new revision."
